  "id": "vasopressin",
  "term": "vasopressin",
  "definition": "Vasopressin is a neuropeptide discussed in autism research as a circulating body chemical related to social behavior. In young autistic children, its levels may differ from typical patterns, and giving vasopressin from outside the body has been reported to improve social symptoms, but its role in language development was not established in this source.",
